{"nodes": [{"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter5_construction_chapter5", "label": "Chapter 5 \u2014 The construction of \u039b", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter5-construction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter5_construction_lambda8", "label": "\u039b\u2088 \u2014 976 cells on eight coordinates, the base object", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter5-construction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter5_construction_eight_coordinates", "label": "The eight coordinates (n, \u2113, k, q, e, f, g, 2S)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter5-construction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Eight is the fewest that pin a transition down once spin coupling is set aside."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter5_construction_seven_constraints_four_origins", "label": "Seven constraints, four origins, and nothing else", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter5-construction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The four-origin table is the whole of the input, printed and auditable in a glance: a single constraint from a fifth source would make it impossible to tell afterward which of \u039b's properties belong to the indexing and which were carried in on that bound."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter5_construction_monotone_bound_form", "label": "Every constraint is of one form \u2014 x\u1d62 \u2264 \u03c6(x\u2c7c), \u03c6 monotone", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter5-construction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not how they happen to be written but forced: a set cut out by a bound summing two coordinates would not be closed, and closure is the one thing the rest of the book cannot do without."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter5_construction_constraint_tree", "label": "The constraint graph is a tree \u2014 treewidth 1", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter5-construction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter5_construction_closure_proof", "label": "\u039b is closed \u2014 join and meet of any two cells are again cells", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter5-construction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every condition reads x\u1d62 \u2264 \u03c6(x\u2c7c) with \u03c6 monotone, so the condition survives taking the larger or smaller value in each slot."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter5_construction_e_lambda_zero", "label": "E(\u039b) = 0 \u2014 verified at four cap settings, and \u211b(\u211b(\u039b)) = \u211b(\u039b)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter5-construction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Checked by direct count at 216, 976, 1,636 and 2,394 cells, so \u039b is a true fixed point rather than closed by luck at one size."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter5_construction_spin_envelope", "label": "The spin envelope 2S \u2264 k \u2014 the one place the object is not exact", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter5-construction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three origins give exact limits; vector coupling gives an envelope met by only 48.5% of the cells it allows. The book states the split rather than tucking it away, and shows the envelope is forced."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter5_construction_caps_note", "label": "A note on caps \u2014 counts move with the caps, shape does not", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter5-construction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter5_construction_tower_definition", "label": "The tower \u039b\u2088 \u2026 \u039b\u2081\u2083 and the order the coupling coordinates are added", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter5-construction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter5_construction_mc_01_pointer", "label": "[MC-01] \u2014 the full closure proof (sublattice of a product of chains, Birkhoff 1940)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter5-construction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter5_construction_figure_5_1", "label": "Figure 5.1 \u2014 eight points, seven lines, no loops", "file_type": "image", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter5-construction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter5_construction_chapter